nL68: \nL69: cast their votes in a secret ballot\nL70: \nL71: b\nL72: \nL73: : the right to vote\nL74: \nL75: were not denied access to the ballot\nL76: \nL77: c\nL78: \nL79: : 【18†vote sense 1a】\nL80: \nL81: … I would cast my ballot as an informed citizen …—Calvin Trillin\nL82: \nL83: 3\nL84: \nL85: a\nL86: \nL87: : the number of votes cast\nL88: \nL89: She won 55 percent of the ballot.\nL90: \nL91: b\nL92: \nL93: : 【19†election sense 1a】\nL94: \nL95: claimed the ballot was rigged\nL96: … the measure … was approved on a second ballot …—William F. Reed\nL97: \nL98: 4\nL99: \nL100: : the drawing of lots\nL101: \nL102: ballot\nL103: \nL104: 2 of 2\nL105: ## 【20†verb】\nL106: \nL107: balloted; balloting; ballots\nL108: \nL109: 【21†intransitive verb】\nL110: \nL111: : to vote or decide by ballot\nL112: \nL113: … members of the House, which earlier had balloted even more massively against the president … voted in their own localized political interests …—The Pittsburgh Press\nL114: \nL115: balloter noun\nL116: \nL117: 【22†Image†prod.cdn-mw.com】\nL118: ## Did you know?\nL119: \nL120: When people voted in ancient Athens, they dropped pebbles into an urn. Similarly, when voting was done by the people of Venice during the Renaissance, secrecy was assured by the use of little colored or marked balls. The Italian word for “little ball” is ballotta, from balla, meaning “ball,” and the diminutive suffix –otta. Now any kind of secret voting, by ball, piece of paper, or voting machine, is called a ballot. So is the right to vote itself.\nL121: ## Synonyms of ballot\nL122: \nL123: Relevance\nL124: \nL125: Noun\nL126: \nL127:   * 【18†vote】\nL128: \nL129: 【17†See All Synonyms & Antonyms in Thesaurus】\nL130: ## Examples of ballot in a Sentence\nL131: \nL132: Noun They cast their votes in a secret ballot. She was elected by secret ballot.\nL133: \nL134: Recent Examples on the Web\nL135: \nL136: Examples are automatically compiled from online sources to show current usage. 【14†Read More】 Opinions expressed in the examples do not represent those of Merriam-Webster or its editors. 【23†Send us feedback†docs.google.com】.\nL137: \nL138: Noun\nL139: Voting by noncitizens and fraud involving mail ballots are both rare. — Aoife Walsh, Washington Post, 27 Oct. 2026 Trump has spent the past month crisscrossing the country, rallying in support of down-ballot Republicans ahead of the 2026 midterm elections. — Christian Datoc, The Washington Examiner, 27 Oct. 2026\nL140: \nL141: Verb\nL142: The Brewers traded third baseman Caleb Durbin and infielders Andruw Monasterio and Anthony Seigler to the Boston Red Sox in February after Durbin had finished third in the NL rookie of the year balloting last season. — ABC News, 17 Oct. 2026 Copenhaver's attorney Bill Bock cited a heavy dose of case law and statute to claim the commission has the authority to investigate voters and that these voters don't have a right to ballot secrecy.\nL143: — Cate Charron, IndyStar, 29 July 2026 【24†See All Example Sentences for ballot】\nL144: ## Word History\nL145: \nL146: Etymology\nL147: \nL148: Noun\nL149: \nL150: Italian ballotta, from Italian dialect, diminutive of balla ball — more at 【25†balloon】\nL151: \nL152: First Known Use\nL153: \nL154: Noun\nL155: \nL156: 1549, in the meaning defined at 【26†sense 1a】\nL157: \nL158: Verb\nL159: \nL160: 1603, in the meaning defined 【27†above】\nL161: \nL162: Time Traveler\nL163: \nL164: The first known use of ballot was in 1549\nL165: \nL166: 【28†See more words from the same year】\nL167: \nL168: ## Browse Nearby Words\nL169: \nL170: 【29†balloon vine】\nL171: \nL172: ballot\nL173: \nL174: 【30†Ballota】\nL175: \nL176: 【31†See all Nearby Words】\nL177: ## Articles Related to ballot\nL178: \nL179: 【32†The History of 'Ballot' Where your vote comes from】 【33†What's a 'downticket candidate'? And what's a 'downballot race'?】\nL180: \nL181: ## Cite this Entry\nL182: \nL183: Style\nL184: \nL185: [Select]\nL186: \nL187: “Ballot.” Merriam-Webster.com Dictionary, Merriam-Webster, https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/ballot. Accessed 2 Nov. 2026.\nL188: \nL189: 【34†Image†prod.cdn-mw.com】Copy Citation\nL190: ## Kids Definition\nL191: \nL192: ballot\nL193: \nL194: 1 of 2 noun\nL195: \nL196: bal·​lot 【16†ˈbal-ət 】\nL197: \nL198: 1\nL199: \nL200: : a small ball or sheet of paper used to cast a secret vote\nL201: \nL202: 2\nL203: \nL204: a\nL205: \nL206: : the action or system of voting\nL207: \nL208: b\nL209: \nL210: : the right to vote\nL211: \nL212: 3\nL213: \nL214: : the number of votes cast\nL215: \nL216: ballot\nL217: \nL218: 2 of 2 verb\nL219: \nL220: : to vote or decide by ballot\nL221: \nL222: Etymology\nL223: \nL224: Noun\nL225: \nL226: from Italian ballotta \"little ball (used in voting),\" from balla \"ball\"\nL227: \nL228: Word Origin\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVOTER Definition & Meaning - Merriam-Webster (https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/voter)\nciteturn36view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/voter\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 164\nL0: 【0†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】 【1†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】\nL1: \nL2: [Input: Search Dictionary]\nL3: \nL4:   * 【2†Games】\nL5:   * 【3†Word of the Day】\nL6:   * 【4†Grammar】\nL7:   * 【5†Word Finder】\nL8:   * 【6†Slang】\nL9:   * 【7†Newsletters】\nL10:   * 【8†Wordplay】\nL11:   * 【9†Rhymes】\nL12:   * 【10†Thesaurus】\nL13:   * 【11†Join MWU†unabridged.merriam-webster.com】\nL14:   * More\nL15:     * 【2†Games】\nL16:     * 【3†Word of the Day】\nL17:     * 【4†Grammar】\nL18:     * 【8†Wordplay】\nL19:     * 【6†Slang】\nL20:     * 【9†Rhymes】\nL21:     * 【5†Word Finder】\nL22:     * 【7†Newsletters】\nL23:     * 【10†Thesaurus】\nL24:     * 【11†Join MWU†unabridged.merriam-webster.com】\nL25:     * Shop\nL26:     * 【12†Books†shop.merriam-webster.com】\nL27:     * 【13†Merch†merriamwebster.threadless.com】\nL28: \nL29: 【14†Diction